# story/02-sabotage.scene — bible.md spine scene 3 (Signs of
# sabotage). Kept lines are cited inline with their source. See
# docs/canon/bible.md and docs/canon/kept.md.

== sabotage_evidence
bg desert_night
> The tull coupling isn't broken. It's rerouted - spliced clean, no scorch, no strain. Whoever did this knew exactly which wire carried the towed half of the train.
check cowboy vs 2
    style -> tracked_expert
    success -> tracked_ok
    tie -> tracked_ok
    fail -> tracked_missed

== tracked_expert
show slim talk left
slim: Splice like that, someone worked this line before. Boots, not a drone.
-> brand_choice

== tracked_ok
slim: Somebody's been here. Recently, and on purpose.
-> brand_choice

== tracked_missed
> Slim misses the print in the dust. The cargo bot doesn't.
cargo_bot: (Sh-query maintenance status sh-current sh-loader)
-> brand_choice

== brand_choice
> Burned into the housing, under the splice: a seal, four words to a chain. (seal (kessa voth sil fen))
choice
    "Read the brand." -> brand_attempt
    "Leave it. It isn't cargo." -> git_blame

== brand_attempt
puzzle read-brand
    pass -> brand_read_pass
    lockout -> brand_read_lockout

== brand_read_pass
set read_brand = true
> Slim works the chain down to the third word, sil, and keeps it.
-> git_blame

== brand_read_lockout
> The brand stays a jumble - kessa, voth, and no way through to the rest.
-> git_blame

== git_blame
if not met_clipi
    show terminal idle right
    terminal: Patch requested. Routing co-pilot Clipi to this channel.
    set met_clipi = true
show clipi talk center
# kept: script.rpy:309
clipi: Running git blame on loader firmware... Last modifications made by user 'cdr_rustler42'.
# kept: script.rpy:357
slim: CDR rustlers! Those parenthesis-thieving varmints!
> Not a jam. A theft, coupled clean into the chain like it belonged there.
-> clipi_check
